  "term": "systemic lupus erythematosus",
  "definition": "Systemic lupus erythematosus is a long-lasting inflammatory connective tissue disorder that tends to flare and recur, often with fever, and can affect multiple body systems, especially the skin, joints, kidneys, and linings around internal organs. Its cause is unknown, but it is thought to involve a breakdown in the body’s normal autoimmune regulation.",
